+# H2.3 Command Governance Policy
+
+## Overview
+
+H2.3 introduces command-class-aware governance that gates execution based on
+command type and completion state.
+
+## Command Classes
+
+1. **Reflex**: `stop`, `cancel`, `mute`
+   - Eligible immediately upon structural stability
+   - No endpoint requirement
+
+2. **Closed-structure**: `focus terminal`, `delete previous token`
+   - Eligible after structural stability (2 consecutive matches)
+   - No endpoint requirement
+
+3. **Parameterized**: `go to line <n>`, `switch tab <n>`, `scroll down <n>`
+   - Requires: structural stability + slot closure + slot stability + endpoint
+   - Hard-gated at final step only
+
+## Gating Logic
+
+```
+if (commandClass === "reflex" || commandClass === "closed_structure") {
+  executionEligible = structurallyStable;
+} else if (commandClass === "parameterized") {
+  executionEligible = structurallyStable && slotClosed && slotStable && slotFinalized;
+}
+```
+
+## Decision Continuity
+
+H2.3 maintains decision continuity via:
+- H23TraceStep per-step recording
+- H23DecisionSummary persisted to JSON
+- chunkId correlation throughout
+
+## Environment Flags
+
+- `H23_HARD_GATE_NUMERIC=true` - Enable strict gating for parameterized commands
